 case that would be  why no branch timeline was ever created  from steve going back in time and  staying with peggy he was actually  always supposed to do that  so really what happened in 2012 with  loki escaping was supposed to happen  because he was supposed to make his way  to he who remains  and like he who remains said he paved  the path for them to get to him  now ultimately when they did get to him  he gave them two choices  take over the tva or kill him and his  evil  variants would come millions of them  infinite amounts of them would come  arloki wanted to think about it but  sylvie who had been fighting her entire  life to get to where she was so that she  could kill whoever was in charge of the  tva  didn't really care she just wanted her  revenge and she took it she killed  he who remains and then kang came loki  makes his way back to the tva and there  is a huge statue of  kang the conqueror and this has pretty  big implications on the future of the  mcu including  one division spider-man no way home and  doctor strange and the multiverse of  madness  now killing he who remains sent the  multiverse back into play there was just  one sacred timeline now there is a  gigantic multiverse and it definitely is  in madness and this could definitely  explain why we never saw doctor strange  in one division  he clearly had a lot to deal with since  loki took place before one division more  than likely doctor strange was trying to  get a grasp on this  multiverse of madness concept however  wanda might actually be the key to  everything because it looks like she is  a nexus being  in marvel comics nexus beans are  keystones of the multiverse and they're  pretty crucial to  its coherence and stability and since  our multiverse looks like it could use  some stability it looks like wanda is  going to be the key  however doctor strange may find it  problematic to try and recruit wanda  as wanda in the post-credits scene heard  her kids  now wanda created her kids ou